# Project rules

## Meta rule — rules go everywhere

Any new or changed project rule must be written into **all** agent rule files at once:

- `CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code)
- `AGENTS.md` (Codex, Zed, Gemini CLI, Jules, Cursor)
- `.cursor/rules/project-rules.mdc` (Cursor, `alwaysApply: true`)
- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (GitHub Copilot)

A rule living in only one file is a bug. Keep the wording the same in all of them.

## Hard rules

- **Commit only when asked.** Run `git add` / `git commit` only when the user asks. Never run
  `git merge`, `git rebase`, `git reset --hard`, `git tag` or any other
  history-rewriting command. Read-only git (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`) is fine.
- **Commit messages:** in Russian, prefer a single line, passive form — "Сделан X", not
  "Сделал X". Short and human: what changed, no filler, no file lists. E.g. "Добавлены
  заметки по тулингу", "Разрешены коммиты по просьбе".
  Never add `Co-Authored-By` or any other co-author/attribution trailers.
- **Stay inside this directory.** Don't touch files or run commands outside the repo root.

## Conventions

- `## ... ##` marks folding code regions, not a regular comment prefix. For comments use `#`.
- Site sources live in `pages/*.md`; `docs/` is generated by the build. Don't edit `docs/*.html` by hand.
- `pages/index.md` uses the portfolio layout (`!LAYOUT portfolio`); its directives are documented in `main.py`.

## Commands

- Build the site: `uv run python main.py build`
- Tests: `uv run pytest -q`
- Git hooks run via prek (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`): `uv run prek install` once after clone
